## FAQs

### Do I need to provide power for the rented AV equipment?

Yes, venue power access needs to be confirmed with us before booking. We do not stock generators, so if your venue has no power access, that has to be solved before delivery day, not discovered on it.

### What happens if it rains during my outdoor event?

We do not rent tents or canopies, so arrange a covered backup area with your venue in advance if rain is a real risk. Our technicians assess conditions on site and place equipment around whatever shelter is available.

### Can rented sound equipment be set up on grass or sand?

Yes. Our crew adapts cable runs and stand placement to the actual ground surface at your venue, whether that is grass, sand, gravel or decking.

### How is setting up sound outdoors different from indoors?

With no walls to reflect sound, open air disperses audio further than an indoor room does, so our PA systems are positioned to project across the space rather than fill a closed room. Wind also affects speaker stand placement and microphone choice.

### How early should I book AV equipment for an outdoor event?

Book at least 24 hours in advance to guarantee availability. For a larger outdoor event with weather and power to plan around, book as early as you can once your date and venue are confirmed.

### Do I need to test the equipment myself before my event starts?

No. Our crew tests every speaker and microphone channel, and syncs any screen or projector with the audio, before your event starts.

### Which package should I book for an outdoor event?

It depends on your guest count and venue. See our [audio visual rental for outdoor events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-outdoor-events/) guide for package fit by venue type, or our [packages page](/packages/) for full details.
